.TH DANBY-FOODCHAIN 1
.SH NAME
danby-foodchain \- plants, herbivores, and carnivores
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/foodchain
.SH MODEL
P' = rP(1-P/K)-aPH;
H' = eaPH-dH-bHC;
C' = fbHC-mC.
.PP
P denotes plants, H herbivores, and C carnivores.  Energy moves upward through
the two consumption terms with conversion efficiencies e and f, while losses
occur independently at each consumer level.
.SH DISPLAY
The three histories make trophic delay visible: a plant change first affects
herbivores and only then carnivores.  Labelled instantaneous bars preserve the
identity and scale of all three trophic levels and can be dragged directly.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag a state bar to alter plants, herbivores, or carnivores.  The eight bottom
tracks set plant growth and capacity, grazing and its conversion, herbivore
death, predation and its conversion, and carnivore death.  Space pauses,
period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The independent model module is
.B /appl/danby/foodchain.b.
Its empty boundary, metadata, and finite initial derivative are tested by
.B temple/danbytest.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/foodchain.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/populations.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-manyspecies (1),
.IR numerics (2)
